    /* CHIPCOMMONA_GSIOCTRL      */ "The 4-byte general serial IO Control register is writable and contains a value of zero at device reset. This register is used to perform indirect accesses to either the SPI or I2C interfaces, depending on the value of the GsioMode field. A SPI or I2C transaction is initiated when StartBusy is set.",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_GSIODATA      */ "The 4-byte GSIO Data register is writable and contains 0x0 at device reset. This register contains 32 bits of data to be written to, or data returned from, the GSIO interface. For GSIO transactions requiring write data, this register should be written before writing the GsioCtrl register. For GSIO transactions returning read data, this register may be read after GsioCtrl.StartBusy is cleared. This register is overwritten by all GSIO commands, either by the read data for read commands or arbitary ...",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_INTMASK       */ "The 4-byte Interrupt Mask register is writable and has a reset value of 0x40.\nThis register selectively enables Chipcommon interrupt requests.\nThis register does not affect the recording of the interrupt status in the IntStatus register.",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_INTSTATUS     */ "The 4-byte Interrupt Status register is writable, has a reset value of zero, and contains the status of Chipcommon interrupt requests.\n The interrupt is not asserted unless the corresponding enable field in the IntMask register is also set to 1.\n All fields in this register other than WDReset are read-only",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_JTAGMASTERCMD */ "The 4-byte JTAG Master Command register is writable and has a reset value of zero.\nThe internal JTAG master issues commands in response to writes to this register.",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_JTAGMASTERCTRL */ "The 4-byte JTAG Master Control register is writable and has a reset value of zero. This register configures the internal JTAG master.",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_JTAGMASTERDATA */ "The 4-byte JTAG Master Data register is writable, has a reset value of zero, and contains the data to be loaded into the target JTAG Data register in JTAG transactions started by accesses to the JtagMasterCmd register. Those transactions write the number of bits specified by JtagMasterCmd.DataWidth from the low bits of this register and replace those same bits with data shifted out from the data register.",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_JTAGMASTERINSTR */ "The 4-byte JTAG Master Instruction register is writable, has a reset value of zero, and contains the data to be loaded into the target JTAG instruction register in JTAG transactions started by accesses to the JtagMasterCmd register. Those transactions write the number of bits specified by JtagMasterCmd.InstrWidth from the low bits of this register and replace those same bits with data shifted out from the instruction register.",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_OTPCTRL       */ "The 4-byte OTP Control register is writable, has a reset value of 0x00, and controls the OTP programming state machine. Note: This register is present only when CoreCapabilities.OTPSize contains a nonzero value. The definition of this register depends on the OTP wrapper type.\nWhen OtpWrapperType is 40nm, the register is defined as follows.",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_OTPCTRL1      */ "The 4-byte OTP Control1 regiser is writable and contains 0x0 at device reset. It is present only when WrapperType? indicates that the core contains a 40nm OTP implementation.",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_OTPLAYOUT     */ "The 4-byte OTP Layout registers is read-only and contains a device-specific value at device reset.",
    /* CHIPCOMMONA_OTPPROG       */ "The 4-byte OTP Program register is writable and has a reset value of zero. The driver writes this register to program, and read back, individual bits in the OTP storage. Accesses to OTP using this register are not affected by OTPStatus.OTPProtect[2:0]. Attempts to program a nonexistent bit are ignored and no error is generated. This register is present only when CoreCapabilities.OTPSize contains a nonzero value.\nThe target bit is addressed by specifying its row and column. To determine these coo ...",
