    /* IPT_DROP_MC_LP_CONFIG     */ "Configurations for Drop MC LP",
    /* IPT_DTQ_0_DQCF_CTRL       */ "Transmit data queue threshold. The IPT stores the data read from the DRAM, before it is sent to the FDT. If the number of 256-byte cells stored in the context is above the threshold, then a flow control is sent to the DQCFs. The flow control is sent only if there is an EOB in the FDT memory (in order to prevent dead locks). This config determines if the EOB affects the Flow control or not.",
    /* IPT_DTQ_1_DQCF_CTRL       */ "Transmit data queue threshold. The IPT stores the data read from the DRAM, before it is sent to the FDT. If the number of 256-byte cells stored in the context is above the threshold, then a flow control is sent to the DQCFs. The flow control is sent only if there is an EOB in the FDT memory (in order to prevent dead locks). This config determines if the EOB affects the Flow control or not.",
    /* IPT_DTQ_CONFIG            */ "DTQ configurations",
    /* IPT_DTQ_DEBUG             */ "Debug per DTQ 0..2 - DTQ non-OCB 0,1,2. 3..5 - DTQ OCB 0,1,2. 6..7 - local 0,1.",
    /* IPT_DTQ_DQCF_TH           */ "Transmit data queue threshold. The IPT stores the data read from the DRAM, before it is sent to the FDT. If the number of 256-byte cells stored in the context is above the threshold, then a flow control is sent to the DQCFs. For the MIX traffic queues, the flow control is sent only if there is an EOB in the FDT memory (in order to prevent dead locks).",
    /* IPT_DTQ_FAB_FC_TH         */ "Configurations for DTQ FC TH. The Tx-Dtq towards the FDT/EGQ Have 4 configurable threshold. Once a threshold is crossed a flow control is set (AF0/1/2/3). FC is sent to the scheduler and may stop dequeue from a DQCF or affect shaper according to the mask. Address: 0-FUC/DEV1 Address: 1-FMC-HP/DEV2 Address: 2-FMC-LP/DEV3",
    /* IPT_DTQ_LOC_FC_TH         */ "Configurations for DTQ FC TH. The Tx-Dtq towards the FDT/EGQ Have 4 configurable threshold. Once a threshold is crossed a flow control is set (AF0/1/2/3). FC is sent to the scheduler and may stop dequeue from a DQCF or affect shaper according to the mask. Address: 0-core0 Address: 1-core1",
    /* IPT_DTQ_MAX_SIZE          */ "Transmit data queue Size. The IPT stores the data read from the DRAM before it is sent to the FDT, in a FIFO with 12 contexts, one context per destination device, duplicated per OCB-ONLY and MIX traffic. The data is stored in a shared memory. The possible context size is programmable. In Single FAP mode (Not Dual FAP mode) the user may give a zero size to the contexts of IPT1 and allow the contexts of IPT0 to take over the entire address space.",
    /* IPT_DTQ_OCB_FC_TH         */ "Configurations for DTQ OCB-ONLY FC TH. The Tx-Dtq towards the FDT/EGQ Have 2 configurable threshold for OCB-ONLY FIFOs Once a threshold is crossed a flow control is set (AF0/1). FC is sent to the scheduler and may stop dequeue from a DQCF. Address: 0-FUC/DEV1 Address: 1-FMC-HP/DEV2 Address: 2-FMC-LP/DEV3 (unused).",
    /* IPT_DTQ_START             */ "Transmit data queue Start address. The IPT stores the data read from the DRAM, before it is sent to the FDT, in a FIFO with 12 contexts. The data is stored in a shared memory. The context memory start address is programmable. In Single FAP mode (Not Dual FAP mode) the user may give a zero size to the contexts of IPT1 and allow the contexts of IPT0 to take over the entire address space.",
    /* IPT_DTQ_TH                */ "Transmit data queue threshold. The IPT stores the data read from the DRAM, before it is sent to the FDT. If the number of 256-byte cells stored in the context is above the threshold, then IPT shaper bandwidth is divided according to the shapers decrease factor configuration.",
