    /* MHOST_0_CSATBFUNNEL_PERIPHID3 */ "Part of the set of Peripheral Identification registers. Contains the RevAnd and Customer Modified fields.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSATBFUNNEL_PERIPHID4 */ "Part of the set of Peripheral Identification registers. Contains part of the designer identity and the memory footprint indicator.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSATBFUNNEL_PRIORITY_CTRL_REG */ "The Priority Control Register defines the order in which inputs are selected. Each 3-bit field represents a priority for each particular slave interface. Location 0 has the priority value for the first slave port. Location 1 is the priority value for the second slave port, Location 2 is the third, down to location 7, which has the priority value of the eighth slave port. Values represent the priority value for each port number. If you want to give highest priority to a particular slave port, the ...",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_ASICCTL     */ "Implementation-defined ASIC control, value written to the register is output on asicctl7:0.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_AUTHSTATUS  */ "Reports what functionality is currently permitted by the authentication interface.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_CLAIMCLR    */ "This register is used in conjunction with Claim Tag Set Register, CLAIMSET. This register forms one half of the Claim Tag value. This location enables individual bits to be cleared, write, and returns the current Claim Tag value, read.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_CLAIMSET    */ "This is used in conjunction with Claim Tag Clear Register, CLAIMCLR. This register forms one half of the Claim Tag value. This location allows individual bits to be set, write, and returns the number of bits that can be set, read.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_COMPID0     */ "A component identification register, that indicates that the identification registers are present.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_COMPID1     */ "A component identification register, that indicates that the identification registers are present. This register also indicates the component class.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_COMPID2     */ "A component identification register, that indicates that the identification registers are present.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_COMPID3     */ "A component identification register, that indicates that the identification registers are present.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_CTIAPPCLEAR */ "The CTI Interrupt Acknowledge Register is write-only. A write to this register causes a channel event to be cleared, corresponding to the bit written to.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_CTIAPPPULSE */ "The CTI Application Pulse Register is write-only. A write to this register causes a channel event pulse, one cticlk period, to be generated, corresponding to the bit written to. The pulse external to the ECT can be extended to multi-cycle by the handshaking interface circuits. This register clears itself immediately, so it can be repeatedly written to without software having to clear it.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_CTIAPPSET   */ "The CTI Application Trigger Set Register is read/write. A write to this register causes a channel event to be raised, corresponding to the bit written to.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_CTICHINSTATUS */ "The CTI Channel In Status Register provides the status of the ctichin inputs.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_CTICHOUTSTATUS */ "The CTI Channel Out Status Register provides the status of the CTI ctichout outputs.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_CTICONTROL  */ "The CTI Control Register enables the CTI.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_CTIGATE     */ "The Gate Enable Register prevents the channels from propagating through the CTM to other CTIs. This enables local cross-triggering, for example for causing an interrupt when the ETM trigger occurs. It can be used effectively with CTIAPPSET, CTIAPPCLEAR, and CTIAPPPULSE for asserting trigger outputs by asserting channels, without affecting the rest of the system. On reset, this register is 0xF, and channel propagation is enabled.",
    /* MHOST_0_CSCTI_CTIINEN0    */ "The CTI Trigger 0 to Channel Enable Register enables the signalling of an event on CTM channels when the core issues a trigger, ctitrigin, to the CTI. Within this register there is one bit for each of the four channels implemented. This register does not affect the application trigger operations.",
