    /* NBIH_HRF_RX_PRD_THRESHOLDS_CONFIG_2 */ "Rx High Rate FIFO (HRF2) Priority Drop thresholds.\n Incoming packet is dropped on input if the level of the Rx FIFO exceeded the configurable threshold for the packet priority. This register defines the thresholds for this mechanism.\n The threshold for the highest priority (3) is constant and equals to the FIFO size minus 1. This means that any high prioirty packet can enter the FIFO if there is room.\n Any threshold can be set to FIFO level minus 1 in order to effectively disable the feature.\n H ...",
    /* NBIH_HRF_RX_USE_EXTENDED_MEM_HRF */ "Configuration Register of data Rx High Rate FIFO (HRF).\n                   Each HRF uses memory of either one or two port-macros for the data stream (not TDM).\n                   If set for HRF 0, it will use 2 PM memories (PM0 and PM2).\n                   If set for HRF1, it will use 2 PM memories (PM3 and PM5).\n                    Otherwise, they use memory of a single port-macro.\n                   Each port-macro has RX memory of 2048 entries of 64B.",
