    /* NBIL_HRF_RX_USE_EXTENDED_MEM_HRF */ "Configuration Register of data Rx High Rate FIFO (HRF).\n                   Each HRF uses memory of either one or two port-macros for the data stream (not TDM).\n                   If set for HRF 0, it will use 2 PM memories (PM0 and PM2).\n                   If set for HRF1, it will use 2 PM memories (PM3 and PM5).\n                    Otherwise, they use memory of a single port-macro.\n                   Each port-macro has RX memory of 2048 entries of 64B.",
