    /* NBIL_RX_ELK_BURSTS_CNT    */ "Count the number of bursts sent to the IHB (with and without error).",
    /* NBIL_RX_ELK_BURST_DROP_CNT */ "Count the bursts dropped by the ELK Rx (due to overflow).",
    /* NBIL_RX_ELK_ERR_BURSTS_CNT */ "Count the number of bursts sent to the IHB marked with error. Those bursts are counted also in the RxElkBurstsCnt.",
    /* NBIL_RX_ELK_OCTETS_CNT    */ "Count the number of bytes sent to the IHB.",
    /* NBIL_RX_ELK_STATUS        */ "Status of Rx ELK buffers.",
    /* NBIL_RX_ENABLE_DATAPATH   */ "Enable Rx datapath before reseting the RMC. Setting a bit in this register to zero blocks writes to the Rx FIFO of the respective port, allowing a clean reset of the RMC. The bit for the relevant port should be set before resetting the RMC and cleared only after taking RMC out of reset.",
    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_ERROR_PM      */ "Debug register for Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) for PMLL.\n                   Shows overflow and underflow indications per port.\n                   If overflow is set, indicates that corresponding Rx FIFO overflowed and data was lost. Notice, in order to clear the overflow idication, new packet must enter the FIFO when the FIFO status is below ThresholdAfterOverflow.",
    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_ERROR_PM_3    */ "Debug register for Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) for PML 0..5.\n                   Shows overflow and underflow indications per port.\n                   If overflow is set, indicates that corresponding Rx FIFO overflowed and data was lost. Notice, in order to clear the overflow idication, new packet must enter the FIFO when the FIFO status is below ThresholdAfterOverflow.",
    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_ERROR_PM_4    */ "Debug register for Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) for PML 0..5.\n                   Shows overflow and underflow indications per port.\n                   If overflow is set, indicates that corresponding Rx FIFO overflowed and data was lost. Notice, in order to clear the overflow idication, new packet must enter the FIFO when the FIFO status is below ThresholdAfterOverflow.",
    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_ERROR_PM_5    */ "Debug register for Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) for PML 0..5.\n                   Shows overflow and underflow indications per port.\n                   If overflow is set, indicates that corresponding Rx FIFO overflowed and data was lost. Notice, in order to clear the overflow idication, new packet must enter the FIFO when the FIFO status is below ThresholdAfterOverflow.",
    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_LEVEL_PM      */ "Debug information for Rx MAC Lane FIFO (MLF) of PMLL.\n                   Shows the number of valid entries currently stored in the buffer.",
