    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_LEVEL_PM_4    */ "Debug information for Rx MAC Lane FIFO (MLF) of PML 0..5.\n                   Shows the number of valid entries currently stored in the buffer.",
    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_LEVEL_PM_5    */ "Debug information for Rx MAC Lane FIFO (MLF) of PML 0..5.\n                   Shows the number of valid entries currently stored in the buffer.",
    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_LLFC_THRESHOLDS_CONFIG */ "Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) n Link Level Flow Control generation thresholds.\n                   Rx QMLF may trigger generation of FC indications to the link partner (either through pause frames or through the OOB interface). This register defines the thresholds for this mechanism.\n                   The same threshold apply to all logical FIFOs of the QMLF.",
    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_MAX_OCCUPANCY */ "Debug information for Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF).\n                   Shows the maximal number of valid entries stored in the buffer since this register was last read.",
    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_PFC_THRESHOLDS_CONFIG */ "Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) n Priority Flow Control generation thresholds.\n                   Rx QMLF may trigger generation of FC indications to the link partner (either through pause frames or through the OOB interface). This register defines the thresholds for this mechanism.\n                   The same threshold apply to all logical FIFOs of the QMLF.",
    /* NBIL_RX_MLF_PRD_THRESHOLDS_CONFIG */ "Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) n Priority Drop thresholds.\n                   Incoming packet is dropped on input if the level of the Rx FIFO exceeded the configurable threshold for the packet priority. This register defines the thresholds for this mechanism.\n                   The threshold for the highest priority (3) is constant and equals to the FIFO size minus 1. This means that any high prioirty packet can enter the FIFO if there is room.\n                   Any threshold can be set to FIFO l ...",
    /* NBIL_RX_NUM_TOTAL_DROPPED_EOPS */ "This counter counts the number of EOPs dropped in all the RX PML NIF ports.",
    /* NBIL_RX_PKT_DROP_COUNTER  */ "Per port Rx Packet drop counter.",
    /* NBIL_RX_PKT_FC_DROP_COUNTER */ "Per RX port counter for flow control packets that are dropped  (pause frames or PFC or Mac control). Register 0 corresponds to nif port 24. Register 99 corresponds to nif port 123.",
    /* NBIL_RX_PKT_FC_ERR_COUNTER */ "Per RX port counter for flow control packets that are marked with error  (pause frames or PFC or Mac control). These packets will be sent to the IRE. NBI cant drop these packets because fc indication arrives after more than 64B, so the packet is already written to the FIFO. We drop . Register 0 corresponds to nif port 24. Register 99 corresponds to nif port 123.",
    /* NBIL_RX_PORTS_SRSTN       */ "Rx MLF Reset.\n                   Active low reset for RMC of NIF ports 24-123. Bit 0 for port 24; bit 99 for port 123. It also resets the per-port transaction counter in NBIH SCH.\n                   This reset does not affect the HRFs (ILKN).\n                   Note: corresponding ports and NBIH ports reset should be configured before changing this reset.",
    /* NBIL_RX_PORT_OVF          */ "RX all ports overflow indication.",
    /* NBIL_RX_PRD_PKT_DROP_CNT  */ "Per-port packet drop counter for Priority Drop module.",
    /* NBIL_RX_PRD_VLAN_ETHERTYPE */ "Ethertype to compare to if the traffic is VLAN. If the Ethertype of the packet equals one of those values, the keys to take the priority from is taken from the packet (4 MSBs of Byte14). Otherwise, the key is taken from the register PrdUntagPcp.",
    /* NBIL_RX_QMLF_CONFIG       */ "Configuration Register of Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF).\n                   There are 7 QMLFs, corresponding to 13 quad-Serdes blocks.",
    /* NBIL_SBUS_BROADCAST_ID    */ "Sbus broadcast ID",
    /* NBIL_SBUS_LAST_IN_CHAIN   */ "Sbus last in chain",
    /* NBIL_SIF_CFG              */ "This register sets the mode of statistics traffic from Jericho to the port-macros. When a port is used for statistics, the corresponding NBI FIFO is bypassed and data is directly received from the statistics module in IQM. Note that the correspoding SerDes will not be available for ILKN or Ethernet data. However, no NBI memory is required for this traffic.",
