    /* NBIL_TX_ENABLE_DATAPATH   */ "Enable Tx datapath before reseting the TMC. Setting a bit in this register to zero blocks writes to the Tx FIFO of the respective port, allowing a clean reset of the TMC. The bit for the relevant port should be set before resetting the TMC and cleared only after taking TMC out of reset.",
    /* NBIL_TX_ERROR_FROM_MEM_DIDNT_PROPAGATE */ "Debug register. Inidcates error from the memory didnt propagate to the port-macro at least once. This is relevant for error initiate, where is some cases the memory is read, but the data is not used. This data will be used next time the memory is read, but another initiate is required. Not relevant for errors from the EGQ or real soft errors in the memory.",
