    /* NIF_GTIMER_CONFIGURATION  */ "The Global timer allows rate measurements.\n Some of the counters at the block may work normally, or according to this global timer.\n While working in global timer mode, the related counters can:\n Set to clear when the counter starts.\n Count for defined period and stop when the time expires.\n The values they reach are saved.\n This timer is used for debug only.",
    /* NIF_INDIRECT_COMMAND      */ "Some of the chip memories and tables may be accessed only by indirect mapping.\n The following registers are used for the indirect mapping process:\n IndirectCommand,\n IndirectCommandAddress, IndirectCommandDataIncrement, IndirectCommandWrData, IndirectCommandRdData.\n The command register holds the instruction for this indirect access operation.",
