    /* NIF_MEM_PTR_ASYNC_FIFO_CLK_RATIO */ "In order to synchronize the fifo pointers a block called nbi_mem_ptr_async_fifo is used. This block hold  the event for defined number of cycles and then synchronize the ptr value to new clock.  This register defines the number of holding cycles and represent the clocks ratio.\n One configuration is used for all PMs, however it will be relevant only for PMLs since at the PMXs dp_clk and core_clk are the same.",
