    /* NIF_RX_ENABLE_DATAPATH    */ "Enable Rx datapath before reseting the RMC. Setting a bit in this register to zero blocks writes to the Rx FIFO of the respective port, allowing a clean reset of the RMC. The bit for the relevant port should be set before resetting the RMC and cleared only after taking RMC out of reset.",
    /* NIF_RX_MLF_ERROR_PM       */ "Debug register for Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) for PM 0..8.\n Shows overflow and underflow indications per port.\n If overflow is set, indicates that corresponding Rx FIFO overflowed and data was lost. Notice, in order to clear the overflow idication, new packet must enter the FIFO when the FIFO status is below ThresholdAfterOverflow.",
    /* NIF_RX_MLF_LEVEL_PM       */ "Debug information for Rx MAC Lane FIFO (MLF) of PMH 0..5.\n Shows the number of valid entries currently stored in the buffer.",
    /* NIF_RX_MLF_LLFC_THRESHOLDS_CONFIG */ "Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) n Link Level Flow Control generation thresholds.\n Rx QMLF may trigger generation of FC indications to the link partner (either through pause frames or through the OOB interface). This register defines the thresholds for this mechanism.\n The same threshold apply to all logical FIFOs of the QMLF.",
    /* NIF_RX_MLF_MAX_OCCUPANCY  */ "Debug information for Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF).\n Shows the maximal number of valid entries stored in the buffer since this register was last read.",
    /* NIF_RX_MLF_PFC_THRESHOLDS_CONFIG */ "Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) n Priority Flow Control generation thresholds.\n Rx QMLF may trigger generation of FC indications to the link partner (either through pause frames or through the OOB interface). This register defines the thresholds for this mechanism.\n The same threshold apply to all logical FIFOs of the QMLF.",
    /* NIF_RX_MLF_PRD_THRESHOLDS_CONFIG */ "Rx Quad MAC Lane FIFO (QMLF) n Priority Drop thresholds.\n Incoming packet is dropped on input if the level of the Rx FIFO exceeded the configurable threshold for the packet priority. This register defines the thresholds for this mechanism.\n The threshold for the highest priority (3) is constant and equals to the FIFO size minus 1. This means that any high prioirty packet can enter the FIFO if there is room.\n Any threshold can be set to FIFO level minus 1 in order to effectively disable the featu ...",
