    /* NIF_RX_REQ_PIPE_0_HIGH_EN */ "Mask for the RX high priority Pipe 0 WFQ.\n All Rx QMLFs that have valid data, send requests to the scheduler (SCH). These requests are masked before they enter the SCH.\n QMLFs 0-8 - PPC prioritirs 0 - 8",
    /* NIF_RX_REQ_PIPE_0_LOW_EN  */ "Mask for the RX low priority Pipe 0 WFQ.\n All Rx QMLFs that have valid data, send requests to the scheduler (SCH). These requests are duplicated and masked before they enter the SCH. This duplication and masking allows to prioritize a certain QMLF so it receives a larger share of the B/W of the IRE bus.\n If bit is set, the corresponding QMLF will participate in the round robin when the QMLF requests to send data.\n Each bit corresponds to a certain QMLF. Due to the duplication, QMLF X has 4 corre ...",
