    /* NIF_RX_SCH_DEBUG_RESULT   */ "Reserved. Debug indications for the SCH.",
    /* NIF_RX_THRESHOLD_AFTER_OVERFLOW_QMLF */ "When the Rx MLF reaches overflow, it flags the last packet written to the FIFO with an error, and stops writing new data to the FIFO.\n The Rx MLF then waits until the FIFO status goes below the value of this register (i.e., waits until enough entries are free) and only then resumes writing new data to the FIFO. This reduces the probability of re-entering overflow shortly after.\n This value MUST be smaller than the FIFO depth.\n Same threshold applies to all RMCs of the QMLF.",
